  {
   "id": 674116,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Conduct a survey of five college students via email, social media, telephone, or in person to learn more about the student demographic. Explain that you are collecting data for a classroom assignment only and will not identify them by name.\n<p>Ask these questions:</p>\n<ol style=\"list-style:upper-alpha;padding-left:1.5em;margin-left:1.5em;\">\n<li>If you could adopt a rescue animal today, what would it be?</li>\n<li>What is the best pizza topping?</li>\n<li>Would you rather sneeze for an hour or have hiccups for an hour?</li>\n<li>Would you rather get $1 million right now or $10,000 per month for a lifetime?</li>\n<li>What is your least favorite food?</li>\n</ol>\n<ul style=\"list-style:none;padding-left:1.5em;margin-left:1.5em;text-indent:-1.8em;\">\n<li>2a. Summarize and report your results in a chart.</li>\n<li>2b. C and D are structurally different questions than A, B, and E. What is different between these questions?</li>\n<li>2c. Can your findings be applied to all college students? Why or why not?</li>\n</ul>",
